# DLNA Media Server Configuration
# 
# This file tells Alpha Player how to connect to DLNA media servers.
# When loaded, you'll enter the DLNA browser to browse and play media.
#
# AUTO-DISCOVERY:
# Leave this file empty or with no url= line to auto-discover
# all DLNA servers on your local network.
#
# MANUAL SERVER:
# Specify a server URL to prioritize that server (auto-discovery
# will still find additional servers):
#
# url=http://192.168.1.100:8200/rootDesc.xml
#
# No authentication required - DLNA uses open local network access.
#
# SUPPORTED SERVERS:
# - Plex (enable DLNA in server settings)
# - Jellyfin (enable DLNA in Dashboard > DLNA)
# - Emby
# - MiniDLNA / ReadyMedia
# - Universal Media Server
# - Windows Media Player Network Sharing
# - Most NAS devices (Synology, QNAP, etc.)
